;; ============================================================================

;; THE OPTIMISTIC PASS  —  port of Simple's `codegen/Opto.java`
;;
;; Interprocedural Sparse Conditional Constant Propagation, and the pass that
;; DISCOVERS the call graph.
;; ============================================================================
;;
;; ## Optimistic vs pessimistic, and why both exist
;;
;; `iterpeeps` is PESSIMISTIC: types start where parsing left them and only fall. It cannot prove a
;; loop-carried value constant, because it must assume the back edge could be anything.
;;
;; This pass is OPTIMISTIC: every type is reset to TOP and rises only as evidence of reachability
;; arrives. A value coming round a back edge contributes NOTHING until that back edge is proven
;; reachable — so `for (i=0; i<1; i++) x=1;` proves `x==1`, which the pessimistic pass cannot.
;;
;; The cost is that an optimistic type is a GUESS until the fixpoint closes. See the trap below.
;;
;; ## The three assertions, which are the correctness argument
;;
;;     resetToTop:  record every node's pessimistic type, then set all types to TOP,
;;                  and put EVERY node on the worklist — most produce better than TOP.
;;
;;     per node:    oval = n._type;  nval = n.compute()
;;                  if oval == nval: continue
;;                  assert oval.isa(nval)        ; MONOTONE: types start high and always fall
;;                  assert nval.isa(pessimistic) ; never FALL WORSE than the pessimistic pass
;;                  n._type = nval               ; note: direct assignment, not setType
;;                  requeue outputs; move deps to worklist
;;
;; The second assertion is the one that catches real bugs: the optimistic answer must be at least
;; as good as the pessimistic one. If it is worse, some `compute` is not monotone and the two passes
;; disagree about the same program.
;;
;; ## The call graph is built LAZILY, and the reason is O(n^2)
;;
;; Simple's own explanation, worth keeping verbatim in spirit: the Call->Fun edges "are not in from
;; the start because they are *too many*; we would get O(n^2) edges. So all along we have been
;; treating them as virtual CFG edges — a FunNode taking a Start input is treated as if every call
;; on the planet might call it. Now we make these CG edges concrete, adding them back as we
;; discover that a call calls a particular function."
;;
;; Three stanzas do the linking, and all three fire from inside the ordinary worklist loop:
;;
;;   1. A node whose new type is a TypeFunPtr: for every non-high Call using it AS ITS FPTR, link.
;;   2. A Call that just came ALIVE (old type high, new type not) whose fptr is a TypeFunPtr: link.
;;   3. A Start whose type is a tuple: link the escaping function pointers to Start, because if an
;;      otherwise-dead function pointer escapes, some future caller might find and call it, so the
;;      function must be treated as alive and called from Start.
;;
;; Because a Fun is a Region and a Parm is a Phi (see src/node/call.coil), each new edge lets
;; argument types flow into the callee THROUGH THE ORDINARY MERGE RULES. There is no separate
;; interprocedural propagation step — that is the payoff of the Fun-is-a-Region design.
;;
;; ## After the fixpoint
;;
;;     1. move everything whose type CHANGED onto the peephole worklist
;;     2. resolve any recursive numeric component left at BOTTOM with no arithmetic mode chosen
;;     3. run iterpeeps again — now with a full call graph, so inlining does better
;;
;; Step 2 exists because a cycle of arithmetic nodes can stabilise at BOTTOM with neither int nor
;; float selected; the mode is then resolved from all available evidence before the peepholes
;; consume the types.
;;
;; ## >>> THE TRAP: A TYPE HERE IS PROVISIONAL <<<
;;
;; During this pass every type is a guess that has not yet closed. A rewrite that acts on one is
;; acting on a guess, and the damage is silent.
;;
;;   - `region-compute` seeds its meet with XCONTROL, so a merge NOBODY HAS ANALYSED reports
;;     "provably unreachable" out of nothing.
;;   - `phi-compute` deliberately skips high paths — load-bearing for loops — which hides
;;     provisionality below any local check.
;;
;; So `ty-proven?` is TRANSITIVE over the whole input cone and is a FIXPOINT test, not a "not TOP"
;; test. A stale LOW type is exactly as provisional as a high one. And a proof-gated rewrite is
;; DEFERRED, never declined: nothing else would re-queue it.
;;
;;     ANY is the ABSENCE of information. Every other high type is a CLAIM someone computed.
;;
;; ## Where TypeScript is discharged
;;
;; This pass is where an annotation stops being a hint. Closed world plus this fixpoint computes
;; what actually flows into each parameter; where that meets the annotation, the guard folds away
;; and the value unboxes. Where it does not, the guard stays and the generic path is retained.
;; TypeScript is unsound — bivariant parameters, `any`, unchecked casts, covariant mutable arrays —
;; so nothing here trusts an annotation it has not proven.
;;
;; STATUS: the optimistic fixed point, proof analysis, finite multi-target call linking,
;; numeric-mode resolution and IterPeeps handoff are implemented. Escaping pointers and loading
;; unresolved cross-unit targets remain explicit unsupported boundaries.
(module aot.codegen.opto)
(import "coil.alloc" :as alloc)
(import "coil.primitive" :as primitive)
(import "coil.arraylist" :use *)
(import "aot.util.panic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.node" :use *)
(import "aot.node.call" :use *)
(import "aot.node.control" :use *)
(import "aot.node.arith" :use *)
(import "aot.node.compare" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.iterpeeps" :use *)
(import "aot.type.type" :use *)

;; Record every pessimistic type, set all types to TOP, and queue every node.
(defn opto-reset-to-top! [] (-> i64)
  (let [cnt (arena-node-count)
        (mut i) 1
        (mut reset) 0]
    (loop (if (> (load i) cnt)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load i))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (n-dead? n)
                            0
                            (do
                              (n-set-pesi-ty! n (n-ty n))
                              (n-force-ty! n TY-TOP)
                              (code-add! n)
                              (set! (mut reset) (+ (load reset) 1)))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load reset)))

;; The optimistic fixpoint, with the monotonicity and not-worse-than-pessimistic assertions.
(defn opto-sccp! [] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut changed) 0]
    (loop (match (code-work-pop!)
            (None [] (break 0))
            (Some [id]
                  (match (arena-node id)
                    (None [] (continue))
                    (Some [n]
                          (if (n-dead? n)
                              (continue)
                              (let [old (n-ty n)
                                    fresh (compute n)]
                                (if (= fresh TY-INVALID)
                                    (panic-i "opto-sccp!: live node computed TY-INVALID; op" (n-op n))
                                    0)
                                (if (= old fresh)
                                    (continue)
                                    (do
                                      ;; Optimistic types start at TOP and fall toward the saved
                                      ;; bottom-up answer, never past it.
                                      (if (not (ty-isa? old fresh))
                                          (panic-i "opto-sccp!: non-monotonic optimistic type; op" (n-op n))
                                          0)
                                      (if (and (!= (n-pesi-ty n) TY-INVALID)
                                               (not (ty-isa? fresh (n-pesi-ty n))))
                                          (panic-i "opto-sccp!: optimistic type fell below pessimistic type; op"
                                                   (n-op n))
                                          0)
                                      (n-force-ty! n fresh)
                                      (opto--link-node! n old fresh)
                                      (code-add-outputs! n)
                                      (n-move-deps-to-worklist! n)
                                      (set! (mut changed) (+ (load changed) 1))
                                      (continue))))))))))
    (load changed)))

;; Is this node's current type established by a closed, stable input cone?  Proof is deliberately
;; a NODE query, never a type query: the same lattice value can be a settled result in one graph and
;; a provisional optimistic guess in another.  This computes the greatest fixed point of locally
;; settled nodes.  Starting live candidates at true is what admits mutually recursive SCCP cycles;
;; repeated elimination removes any cycle that reaches an unstable or queued producer.
(defn n-proven? [(target (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        cnt (arena-node-count)
        (mut proven) (al-new [bool] a)
        (mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (> (load i) cnt)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (push! [bool] (mut proven) false)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (set-mid-assert! true)
    (set! (mut i) 1)
    (loop (if (> (load i) cnt)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load i))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (or (n-dead? n)
                                (= (n-ty n) TY-INVALID)
                                (= (n-ty n) TY-TOP)
                                (code-on-worklist? (n-nid n))
                                (!= (compute n) (n-ty n)))
                            0
                            (set! (mut proven) (n-nid n) true)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (let [(mut changed) true]
      (loop (if (not (load changed))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (set! (mut changed) false)
                  (set! (mut i) 1)
                  (loop (if (> (load i) cnt)
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (if (not (get (load proven) (load i)))
                                  0
                                  (match (arena-node (load i))
                                    (Some [n]
                                          (let [nins (n-nins n)
                                                (mut j) 0
                                                (mut ok) true]
                                            (loop (if (or (>= (load j) nins) (not (load ok)))
                                                      (break 0)
                                                      (do
                                                        (match (n-in n (load j))
                                                          (Some [input]
                                                                (if (get (load proven) (n-nid input))
                                                                    0
                                                                    (set! (mut ok) false)))
                                                          ;; Null control/memory/RPC slots are part of
                                                          ;; several final node shapes and carry no
                                                          ;; provisional producer.
                                                          (None [] 0))
                                                        (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                                                        (continue))))
                                            (if (load ok)
                                                0
                                                (do
                                                  (set! (mut proven) (load i) false)
                                                  (set! (mut changed) true)
                                                  0))))
                                    (None [] 0)))
                              (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                              (continue))))
                  (continue)))))
    (set-mid-assert! false)
    (let [answer
            (if (or (n-dead? target) (> (n-nid target) cnt))
                false
                (get (load proven) (n-nid target)))]
      (al-free! [bool] (mut proven))
      answer)))

;; Final Simple triggers linking for ANY node that acquires a TypeFunPtr, not only a literal
;; FunPtrNode. A Phi, Parm or call result can reveal new targets. Also link when a Call first
;; becomes live, even if its pointer's type did not change on that worklist turn.
(defn opto--link-node! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (old i64) (fresh i64)] (-> i64)
  (do
    (if (ty-funptr? fresh)
        (let [count (n-nouts n) (mut i) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load i) count)
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (match (n-out n (load i))
                        (Some [use]
                              (if (and (= (n-op use) OP-CALL)
                                       (n-same? (call-fptr use) n)
                                       (not (ty-high? (n-ty use))))
                                  (opto-link-cg! use fresh) 0))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        0)
    (if (and (= (n-op n) OP-CALL) (ty-high? old) (not (ty-high? fresh)))
        (opto-link-cg! n (n-ty (call-fptr n)))
        0)))

;; Make one virtual call-graph edge concrete: link this call site to the functions its function
;; pointer names. Simple first rejects arity mismatches, then defers complemented/infinite sets,
;; then looks up each finite fidx without purging temporarily dead functions. Link only missing
;; edges and wake the Fun/Parm work. Our register is compilation-local; a missing finite owner is
;; an unresolved unit, NOT an external function invented from absence. Escape handling is separate.
(defn opto-link-cg! [(c (dyn NodeOps)) (tfp i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (not (ty-funptr? tfp))
      0
      (if (or (!= (ty-sig-nargs (ty-funptr-sig tfp)) (call-nargs c))
              (ty-funptr-high? tfp))
          0
          (let [count (ty-funptr-target-count tfp) (mut i) 0 (mut linked) 0]
            (loop (if (>= (load i) count)
                      (break 0)
                      (let [fidx (ty-funptr-target-at tfp (load i))]
                        (match (arena-function fidx)
                          (None []
                                (unimplemented "unresolved finite function-index target"
                                               "src/codegen/compunit.coil — cross-unit resolution"))
                          (Some [fun]
                                (if (or (not (fun-linkable? fun)) (call-linked? c fun))
                                    0
                                    (do
                                      (call-link! c fun)
                                      (code-add! fun)
                                      (code-add-outputs! fun)
                                      (set! (mut linked) (+ (load linked) 1))))))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue))))
            (load linked)))))

;; An escaping function pointer must be treated as alive and called from Start.
(defn opto-link-start! [] (-> i64)
  (do (unimplemented "opto-link-start!" "S4 — src/codegen/opto.coil") 0))

;; Hand every live node to the peephole phase after SCCP. Output-type equality is not enough to
;; skip a node: an input can sharpen and enable idealize while the consumer's computed type remains
;; identical. Final Simple therefore queues the full reachable graph unconditionally.
(defn opto-move-changes-to-worklist! [] (-> i64)
  (let [cnt (arena-node-count)
        (mut i) 1
        (mut moved) 0]
    (loop (if (> (load i) cnt)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load i))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (n-dead? n)
                            0
                            (do (code-add! n) (set! (mut moved) (+ (load moved) 1)))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load moved)))

;; Resolve a recursive numeric component left at BOTTOM with no arithmetic mode selected.
(defn opto-resolve-numeric-modes! [] (-> i64)
  (let [cnt (arena-node-count)
        (mut i) 1
        (mut resolved) 0]
    (loop (if (> (load i) cnt)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load i))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (or (n-dead? n) (!= (opto--mode n) MODE-UNKNOWN))
                            0
                            (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
                                  (mut seen) (al-new [bool] a)
                                  (mut j) 0]
                              (loop (if (> (load j) cnt)
                                        (break 0)
                                        (do
                                          (push! [bool] (mut seen) false)
                                          (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                                          (continue))))
                              (let [evidence (opto--numeric-evidence n (mut seen))]
                                (if (= evidence 0)
                                    0
                                    (do
                                      ;; Bit 2 is float evidence and wins over convertible integer
                                      ;; evidence, exactly as in Simple.
                                      (opto--set-mode! n
                                                       (if (!= (primitive/iand evidence 2) 0)
                                                           MODE-FLT
                                                           MODE-INT))
                                      (code-add! n)
                                      (set! (mut resolved) (+ (load resolved) 1))))
                                (al-free! [bool] (mut seen))))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load resolved)))

;; Numeric-mode virtual dispatch for the node families that carry Simple's one-shot `_mode`.
;; `-1` means this node has no arithmetic mode and must not be considered a candidate.
(defn opto--mode [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [op (n-op n)]
    (if (= op OP-ADD)
        (add-mode n)
        (if (= op OP-SUB)
            (sub-mode n)
            (if (= op OP-MUL)
                (mul-mode n)
                (if (= op OP-DIV)
                    (div-mode n)
                    (if (= op OP-MINUS)
                        (minus-mode n)
                        (if (or (= op OP-EQ) (= op OP-NE) (= op OP-LT) (= op OP-LE))
                            (cmp-mode n)
                            -1))))))))

(defn opto--set-mode! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (mode i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [op (n-op n)]
    (if (= op OP-ADD)
        (add-set-mode! n mode)
        (if (= op OP-SUB)
            (sub-set-mode! n mode)
            (if (= op OP-MUL)
                (mul-set-mode! n mode)
                (if (= op OP-DIV)
                    (div-set-mode! n mode)
                    (if (= op OP-MINUS)
                        (minus-set-mode! n mode)
                        (if (or (= op OP-EQ) (= op OP-NE) (= op OP-LT) (= op OP-LE))
                            (cmp-set-mode! n mode)
                            0))))))))

;; Gather evidence through precisely the recursive node shapes Simple permits.  The visited bitmap
;; makes self- and mutually-recursive Phi/Return/CallEnd components finite.
(defn opto--numeric-evidence [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (seen (mut (ArrayList bool)))] (-> i64)
  (if (or (n-dead? n) (get (load seen) (n-nid n)))
      0
      (do
        (set! (mut seen) (n-nid n) true)
        (let [t (n-ty n)]
          (if (ty-flt? t)
              2
              (if (ty-int? t)
                  1
                  (let [op (n-op n)
                        own (opto--mode n)]
                    (if (> own 0)
                        own
                        (if (and (= op OP-PROJ)
                                 (= (proj-idx n) RETURN-VALUE)
                                 (match (n-in n 0)
                                   (Some [multi] (= (n-op multi) OP-CALLEND))
                                   (None [] false)))
                            ;; A result projection has no data inputs of its own. Its evidence is in
                            ;; each Return linked to the CallEnd it projects.
                            (match (n-in n 0)
                              (Some [cend]
                                    (let [cnt (n-nins cend)
                                          (mut i) 1
                                          (mut evidence) 0]
                                      (loop (if (>= (load i) cnt)
                                                (break 0)
                                                (do
                                                  (match (n-in cend (load i))
                                                    (Some [ret]
                                                          (set! (mut evidence)
                                                                (primitive/ior (load evidence)
                                                                               (opto--numeric-evidence ret
                                                                                                       (mut seen)))))
                                                    (None [] 0))
                                                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                                  (continue))))
                                      (load evidence)))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (if (or (= op OP-PHI)
                                    (= op OP-PARM)
                                    (= op OP-RETURN)
                                    (= op OP-CALLEND)
                                    (>= own 0))
                                (let [cnt (n-nins n)
                                      (mut i) 1
                                      (mut evidence) 0]
                                  (loop (if (>= (load i) cnt)
                                            (break 0)
                                            (do
                                              (match (n-in n (load i))
                                                (Some [input]
                                                      (set! (mut evidence)
                                                            (primitive/ior (load evidence)
                                                                           (opto--numeric-evidence input (mut seen)))))
                                                (None [] 0))
                                              (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                              (continue))))
                                  (load evidence))
                                0))))))))))

;; The whole pass: reset, sccp, move changes, resolve modes, re-peephole.
(defn opto-run! [] (-> i64)
  (do
    (opto-reset-to-top!)
    (let [changed (opto-sccp!)]
      (opto-move-changes-to-worklist!)
      (opto-resolve-numeric-modes!)
      (iter-run!)
      changed)))
